    {
      "id": "gwnote_t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4674.0,
      "y": 1084.0,
      "width": 1192,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "frame_3",
      "index": "b1H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 453209983,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 60116074,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793750000000,
      "created": 1793750000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The old system can't limit what anyone does, so the gateway does it:\n- The agent reads from a copy of the old system made every night, never from the live system\n- Only the gateway knows the old system's password; the agent never sees it. If the old system allows one more\n  user, give the gateway its own\n- The gateway decides who can suggest an entry and who can approve it, so one person always suggests and a\n  different person approves\n- Before writing, it checks the entry (e.g. RV-25-1184) isn't already in the old system, so trying again never\n  creates a copy\n- It allows only refund vouchers and bank-detail changes: no deleting, no changing old entries, and a limit on the\n  amount\n- Every night it compares the old system's list of entries with its own record, and flags any entry someone made\n  directly with the shared login\n- Its limit: anyone with the shared login can still go around it. The real fix, giving each person their own login,\n  is the college's decision",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "gwnote",
      "originalText": "The old system can't limit what anyone does, so the gateway does it:\n- The agent reads from a copy of the old system made every night, never from the live system\n- Only the gateway knows the old system's password; the agent never sees it. If the old system allows one more\n  user, give the gateway its own\n- The gateway decides who can suggest an entry and who can approve it, so one person always suggests and a\n  different person approves\n- Before writing, it checks the entry (e.g. RV-25-1184) isn't already in the old system, so trying again never\n  creates a copy\n- It allows only refund vouchers and bank-detail changes: no deleting, no changing old entries, and a limit on the\n  amount\n- Every night it compares the old system's list of entries with its own record, and flags any entry someone made\n  directly with the shared login\n- Its limit: anyone with the shared login can still go around it. The real fix, giving each person their own login,\n  is the college's decision",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
